    {
      "id": "king-richard-the-second/sceneI_28.2/p@15426",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "GAUNT.\nAlas, the part I had in Woodstock’s blood\nDoth more solicit me than your exclaims\nTo stir against the butchers of his life.\nBut since correction lieth in those hands\nWhich made the fault that we cannot correct,\nPut we our quarrel to the will of heaven,\nWho, when they see the hours ripe on earth,\nWill rain hot vengeance on offenders’ heads.",
